+For `software` projects, the template seeds default architecture conventions under `## Conventions`:
+- `SRP & High Cohesion`: one file/module = one clear responsibility. High cohesion, low coupling. If an entity does two things, split it.
+- `Service Layer & Anti-Corruption`: isolate third-party libraries and external APIs behind wrappers/interfaces. Domain logic depends on interfaces, not vendors (Dependency Inversion).
+- `Composition over inheritance`: extract shared logic into injectable utils/services/helpers; avoid deep inheritance trees.
+- `Testability by default`: lean on small interfaces, pure functions, and injectable dependencies.
+- `Pragmatic KISS/YAGNI`: start simple and direct; abstract only when there are 2+ consumers, 2+ vendors, or test requirements demand it.
